  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive). Pattern: X⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{止|や}む (X stops).\n\nASPECT: て⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ indicates ongoing cessation is not applicable; the focus is on the moment of stopping.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{雨|あめ}→雨：00583_ame⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{止|や}む (rain stops)\n- ⟦{風|かぜ}→風：00641_kaze⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{止|や}む (wind stops)\n- {止|や}まない (doesn't stop)\n- {止|や}みそう (looks like it will stop)\n- {止|や}む⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{得|え}ない→得る：02014_eru⟧ (unavoidable, can't be helped)\n\nPRIMARY USAGE: Mainly used for natural phenomena (rain, wind, snow) and abstract things (pain, crying).\n\nSET EXPRESSION: {止|や}む⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{得|え}ない→得る：02014_eru⟧ (unavoidable, having no choice) is a very common fixed phrase.\n\nCONTRAST WITH ⟦{止|と}まる→止まる：00555_tomaru⟧:\n- {止|や}む: natural cessation (rain stops, wind dies down)\n- ⟦{止|と}まる→止まる：00555_tomaru⟧: stopping of movement (car stops, clock stops)",
